Absolutely! Here’s a robust PHP function for device detection using the User-Agent string. This covers most common cases for smartphones, tablets, and desktops, and is inspired by open-source logic (like Mobile Detect) but simplified for your use case.

---

## Robust PHP Device Detection Function

```php
function detectDeviceType($userAgent) {
    $userAgent = strtolower($userAgent);

    // Tablet detection
    $tabletKeywords = [
        'ipad', 'tablet', 'kindle', 'playbook', 'silk', 'nexus 7', 'nexus 9', 'nexus 10',
        'sm-t', 'gt-p', 'tab', 'xoom', 'sch-i800', 'touchpad', 'kfapwi', 'kftt', 'kfjwa', 'kfjwi'
    ];
    foreach ($tabletKeywords as $keyword) {
        if (strpos($userAgent, $keyword) !== false) {
            return 'tablet';
        }
    }
    // Android tablets (Android but not Mobile)
    if (strpos($userAgent, 'android') !== false && strpos($userAgent, 'mobile') === false) {
        return 'tablet';
    }

    // Smartphone detection
    $smartphoneKeywords = [
        'iphone', 'ipod', 'android', 'blackberry', 'bb10', 'mini', 'windows ce', 'palm', 'mobile',
